  "name": "@forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp",
  "readme": "# Podio MCP Server\n\n[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)\n[![npm package](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp.svg?style=flat-square)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp)\n[![Node.js Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/node-\u226524.0.0-brightgreen.svg)](https://nodejs.org/)\n[![TypeScript](https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-5.9+-blue.svg)](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)\n\nA Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that integrates Podio with Claude, enabling natural language management of Podio items and tasks. Automate workflows, manage projects, and organize work with conversational AI.\n\n## Features\n\n- **OAuth2 Authentication** - Secure authentication with automatic token refresh\n- **CRUD Operations** - Create, read, update, and delete Podio items and tasks\n- **Intelligent Caching** - App structure caching with automatic refresh for performance\n- **AI-Powered Suggestions** - Smart project/epic suggestions using fuzzy matching\n- **Multi-Workspace Support** - Works with any Podio workspace using explicit coordinates\n- **Comprehensive Search** - Search items, tasks, files, and conversations across scopes\n- **Notification Management** - Manage and filter Podio notifications\n- **Activity Tracking** - Full comment and revision history for items\n- **File Attachments** - Upload local files and attach them to items or comments\n- **Robust Error Handling** - Detailed error messages for debugging\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| **Runtime** | Node.js 24+ / Bun |\n| **Language** | TypeScript 5.9+ |\n| **Protocol** | Model Context Protocol SDK ^0.7.0 |\n| **Testing** | Jest 30 |\n| **Code Quality** | Biome 2.3+ (linting & formatting) |\n| **Documentation** | TypeDoc |\n| **Package Manager** | npm / Bun |\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- **Node.js** \u2265 24.0.0 or **Bun** \u2265 1.0.0\n- Podio account with API credentials (see [Setup Guide](docs/setup-guide.md))\n- MCP-compatible client (Claude Desktop, Cline, etc.)\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Install\n\n```bash\nbunx @forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp\n```\n\n### Configure\n\nAdd to your MCP client configuration (`.mcp.json` or Claude Desktop config):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"podio-mcp\": {\n      \"command\": \"bunx\",\n      \"args\": [\"@forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"PODIO_CLIENT_ID\": \"${PODIO_CLIENT_ID}\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis uses Podio's implicit OAuth flow, which only needs a Client ID. To use the auth-code flow instead, add `PODIO_CLIENT_SECRET` to the `env` block. `PODIO_REDIRECT_URI` is optional \u2014 the package defaults to `http://localhost:8080/callback`; override it only if your Podio app is registered with a different redirect URI.\n\n#### Claude Code one-liner\n\nRegister the server at project scope so credentials stay in `.mcp.json` rather than `~/.claude.json`. The single-quoted `<<'EOF'` delimiter keeps the `${VAR}` references literal \u2014 Claude Code expands them at spawn time, so no secrets are written to disk:\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add-json --scope project podio-mcp \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"command\": \"bunx\",\n  \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@forumviriumhelsinki/podio-mcp\"],\n  \"env\": {\n    \"PODIO_CLIENT_ID\": \"${PODIO_CLIENT_ID}\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nAfter running, verify the file contains the literal placeholder, not an expanded value:\n\n```bash\ngrep PODIO_CLIENT_ID .mcp.json\n# Expected: \"PODIO_CLIENT_ID\": \"${PODIO_CLIENT_ID}\"\n```\n\nAdd `-s user` before the name to install at user scope (`~/.claude.json`) instead. Drop any `PODIO_*` lines you don't have set \u2014 empty strings would otherwise override the package's built-in `PODIO_REDIRECT_URI` default.\n\nGet your API credentials from [Podio Developers](https://developers.podio.com/api-key).\n\n### Usage Examples\n\n```\n# Load an app structure for querying\nLoad app structure for myorg/myspace/myapp\n\n# Query items with filters\nShow me all items with status \"In Progress\"\n\n# Create new items\nCreate a new item titled \"Review pull request\" with description \"Urgent PR\"\n\n# Search across workspace\nSearch for items containing \"authentication\" in myspace\n\n# Manage tasks\nCreate a task assigned to [redacted-email:ff8d9819fc0e] due tomorrow\n\n# Get notifications\nShow my unread notifications from the last 7 days\n```\n\nSee [Usage Examples](docs/usage-examples.md) for more detailed workflows.\n\n## Comment Formatting\n\nPodio renders comment bodies as **Markdown**. `create_item_comment` and\n`update_comment` pass your text through unchanged, so a comment written as\nplain text can render differently from what you wrote.\n\nVerified against a rendered Podio comment:\n\n| Syntax | Renders as |\n|---|---|\n| `**bold**` | bold |\n| `*italic*` | italic |\n| `` `inline code` `` | monospace |\n| `- item` | bullet list |\n| `1. item` | ordered list \u2014 **see the caveat below** |\n\n### Numbered lines are one continuous list\n\nPodio treats *every* line beginning with `N.` in a comment as belonging to a\nsingle ordered list, and renumbers them sequentially \u2014 even when the lines are\nparagraphs apart and you meant them as section headings. Numbers you did not\nwrite appear, and the ones you did write disappear:\n\n```\nYou write:            Podio renders:\n\n1. COSTS              1. COSTS\n...                   ...\n2. THE CHANGE         13. TWO THINGS THAT LOOK LIKE WASTE\n...                   16. OPEN QUESTIONS\n7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n```\n\nUse `**Bold headings**` or `- ` bullets for sections instead. If you genuinely\nwant an ordered list, keep it to one contiguous block.\n\nUntested (avoid unless you verify in the browser): `##` headings, tables and\nblockquotes.\n\n## File Attachments\n\nPodio treats uploading a file and attaching it as two separate operations, and\nthe MCP surface mirrors that:\n\n| Step | Tool | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Upload | `upload_file(file_path, filename?)` | Returns a `file_id`. Takes a **path on the machine running this server**, not file contents. Max 100 MB. |\n| 2a. Attach to an item | `attach_file(file_id, item_id)` | Adds the file to the item's attachments. |\n| 2b. Attach to a comment | `create_item_comment(item_id, text, file_ids)` | Comments must be created *with* their files \u2014 see below. |\n\nA freshly uploaded file is **unattached**: it has an ID, but nothing links to\nit until step 2. Stopping after `upload_file` leaves a file nobody can reach.\n\nAttaching to a comment is not a second call, because a comment has no ID to\nattach to until it exists \u2014 so its files are named by `file_ids` at creation\ntime. That is Podio's ordering, not a limitation of this server.\n\nItem attachments live on the item itself, **not** in a file-type app field, so\n`attach_file` works even when `get_app_structure` reports no file field for the\napp.\n\n```\n# Post a generated report to a ticket\nUpload /tmp/q3-report.html, then attach it to item 3246190585\n\n# Or deliver it with a comment in one exchange\nUpload /tmp/q3-report.html and comment \"Q3 report attached\" on item 3246190585\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\npodio-mcp/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 index.ts                 # Main MCP server\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 oauth-helper.ts          # OAuth2 authentication\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 api/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 podio-api-client.ts  # Podio HTTP client\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 services/                # Business logic layer\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 items/               # Item CRUD operations\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 tasks/               # Task management\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 comments/            # Comment handling\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 search/              # Search functionality\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 app/                 # App structure discovery\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 notifications/       # Notification management\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 project-epic/        # Project/epic suggestions\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 handlers/                # Tool-call handlers extracted from index.ts\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 tools/                   # Tool schemas / registration\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 fields/                  # Podio field-shape converters\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cache/                   # Caching layer\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 config/                  # Build-time defaults injected at publish\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 errors/                  # Custom error types\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils/                   # Cross-cutting helpers\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 types/                   # TypeScript definitions\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 __tests__/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 unit/                    # Unit tests\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 integration/             # Integration tests\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 fixtures/                # Test data and mocks\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 docs/                        # Documentation\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 scripts/                     # Build and configuration scripts\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 build/                       # Compiled output (generated)\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Build & Run\n\n```bash\n# Development with watch mode\nbun run dev\n\n# Build production bundle\nbun run build\n\n# Run the server\nbun run start\n\n# Generate configuration\nbun run configure\n```\n\n### Code Quality\n\n```bash\n# Lint with Biome\nbun run lint\n\n# Auto-fix lint issues\nbun run lint:fix\n\n# Format code\nbun run format\n\n# Check formatting\nbun run format:check\n\n# Run all checks (CI mode)\nbun run check\n```\n\n### Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\nbun test\n\n# Run with coverage report\nbun run test:coverage\n\n# Watch mode for development\nbun run test:watch\n\n# Unit tests only\nbun run test:unit\n\n# Integration tests only\nbun run test:integration\n```\n\n### Documentation\n\n```bash\n# Generate TypeDoc API documentation\nbun run docs\n\n# Watch mode with live reload\nbun run docs:serve\n\n# Build everything including docs\nbun run docs:build\n\n# Deploy documentation\nbun run docs:deploy\n```\n\n## Documentation\n\n- **[Setup Guide](docs/setup-guide.md)** - Installation, configuration, and troubleshooting\n- **[Usage Examples](docs/usage-examples.md)** - Commands and workflow patterns\n- **[API Documentation](docs/API_DOCUMENTATION.md)** - Architecture and API details\n- **[Notifications Guide](docs/NOTIFICATIONS.md)** - Notification management\n- **[Live Docs](https://forumviriumhelsinki.github.io/podio-mcp/)** - Generated API reference\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n| Variable | Description | Required |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| `PODIO_CLIENT_ID` | Podio API Client ID | Yes \u2014 register your own Podio app at [Podio Developers](https://developers.podio.com/api-key) and set this |\n| `PODIO_CLIENT_SECRET` | Podio API Client Secret | No (presence enables auth-code flow; absence selects implicit flow) |\n| `PODIO_REDIRECT_URI` | OAuth redirect URI | No (defaults to `http://localhost:8080/callback`) |\n| `PODIO_NON_INTERACTIVE` | Set to `1` to fail with an actionable error instead of opening a browser when re-authentication is required | No (defaults to interactive) |\n| `PODIO_DEBUG` | Enable debug logging | No |\n\nSet `PODIO_NON_INTERACTIVE=1` for scheduled jobs, CI, and unattended servers.\nWithout it, a server that needs re-authentication binds the OAuth callback port\nand waits up to three minutes for a browser redirect \u2014 which, with nobody there\nto complete it, looks to the caller like a tool call that never returns.\n\n## Contributing\n\nWe welcome contributions! Please follow these steps:\n\n1. **Fork** the repository\n2. **Create a feature branch** (`git checkout -b feat/your-feature`)\n3. **Write tests first** (TDD approach) and implement functionality\n4. **Run the test suite** (`bun test`) and check coverage\n5. **Format and lint** your code (`bun run format && bun run lint:fix`)\n6. **Commit** with [conventional commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):\n   - `feat(scope): description` - New features\n   - `fix(scope): description` - Bug fixes\n   - `docs: description` - Documentation changes\n   - `test: description` - Test additions\n   - `chore: description` - Maintenance\n7. **Push** to your fork and **submit a pull request**\n\nSee the [Testing Guide](./.claude/rules/testing.md) for detailed testing practices.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nEncounter an issue? Check the [Setup Guide Troubleshooting](docs/setup-guide.md#troubleshooting) section or [create an issue](https://github.com/ForumViriumHelsinki/podio-mcp/issues) with:\n- Error message and stack trace\n- Steps to reproduce\n- Environment (Node.js version, OS)\n- MCP client being used\n\n## License\n\nMIT License - see [LICENSE](LICENSE) for details.\n\n## Support\n\n- [Troubleshooting Guide](docs/setup-guide.md#troubleshooting)\n- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/ForumViriumHelsinki/podio-mcp/issues)\n- [Podio API Documentation](https://developers.podio.com/doc)\n",
